        "subject": "LU-17000 ldlm: report allocation failures from ldlm_setup()",
        "message": "LU-17000 ldlm: report allocation failures from ldlm_setup()\n\nGOTO(label, rc) does not assign its second argument, so the three\nbare GOTO(out, -ENOMEM) sites left rc at 0.  ldlm_setup() then ran\nldlm_cleanup(), which frees ldlm_state, and still reported success,\nleaving ldlm_refcount at 1 with a NULL ldlm_state for the next\ncaller to dereference.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 1196bd199e7c (\"LU-8066 ldlm: move /proc/fs/lustre/ldlm to sysfs\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ibaccef3294deb5130e6d8fe8299678ab36c6076a\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68245\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
